{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"O50330","secondaryAccessions":["Q2NKG6","Q937J2"],"uniProtkbId":"TRWK_ECOLX","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2026-01-28","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-11-04","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2002-06-01","entryVersion":88,"sequenceVersion":2},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Escherichia coli","taxonId":562,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Gammaproteobacteria","Enterobacterales","Enterobacteriaceae","Escherichia"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Type IV secretion system ATPase TrwK"},"ecNumbers":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23035111"}],"value":"3.6.4.6"}]}},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"EMBL","id":"CAA57024.2"}],"value":"trwK"},"synonyms":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"35732732"}],"value":"virB4"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P0A3W0"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23035111"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23852869"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"35732732"}],"value":"Component of the Trw type IV secretion system (T4SS), which is involved in bacterial conjugation of plasmid R388, a conjugative plasmid that confers resistance to sulfonamide and trimethoprim (PubMed:35732732). The TrwK subunit provides energy for pilus biogenesis and substrate transfer (PubMed:23852869). It shows ATPase activity (PubMed:23035111). It can act as a dislocation motor to catalyze extraction of TrwL/VirB2 pilin monomers from the inner membrane during T4SS biogenesis, probably through ATP binding/hydrolysis, and acts synergistically with TrwD/VirB11 to induce a structural change in the pilin (By similarity). Binds DNA, with a higher affinity for G4 quadruplex structures than for single-stranded DNA (PubMed:23035111). It can inhibit the DNA-dependent ATPase activity of TrwB (PubMed:23035111)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"ATP + H2O = ADP + phosphate + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:13065"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15377"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:30616"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:43474"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:456216"}],"ecNumber":"3.6.4.6","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23035111"}]},"physiologicalReactions":[{"directionType":"left-to-right","reactionCrossReference":{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:13066"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"23035111"}]}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23035111"}],"value":"The ATPase activity is not affected by addition of ssDNA or G4 DNA"}],"commentType":"ACTIVITY REGULATION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23035111"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23852869"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28923826"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"35732732"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"37814112"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"38886579"}],"value":"The core secretion machinery of the Trw T4SS is composed of cytoplasmic ATPases that form the energy center, an inner membrane complex (IMC), an outer membrane core complex (OMCC) and a stalk (or cylinder) that connects the IMC and the OMCC (PubMed:28923826, PubMed:35732732, PubMed:37814112, PubMed:38886579). This subunit forms a hexamer of dimers (PubMed:35732732, PubMed:38886579). One subunit in each of the 6 dimers forms a central hexamer, the second subunit of the dimers protrudes out (PubMed:35732732, PubMed:38886579). Forms a hexameric double ring (PubMed:23035111). Interacts with TrwB/VirD4 and TrwD/VirB11 (PubMed:23852869, PubMed:28923826)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O50330","intActId":"EBI-16098189"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"O50329","geneName":"trwM","intActId":"EBI-16098241"},"numberOfExperiments":5,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"28923826"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"35732732"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"38886579"}],"value":"Cell inner membrane","id":"SL-0037"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"35732732"}],"value":"Single-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9904"},"orientation":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"35732732"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"38886579"}],"value":"Cytoplasmic side","id":"SL-9910"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the TrbE/VirB4 family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":823,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Type IV secretion system ATPase TrwK","featureId":"PRO_0000462755"},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":37,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Periplasmic","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"35732732"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":38,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":60,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"35732732"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0007744","source":"PDB","id":"7OIU"}]},{"type":"Topological domain","loca